
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -e
# create_realone_repo.sh
# Usage: bash create_realone_repo.sh
# This script will create a folder RealOneOS, populate all files, init git, and zip it.

ROOT="RealOneOS"
if [ -d "$ROOT" ]; then
  echo "Removing existing $ROOT (backup first if needed)..."
  rm -rf "$ROOT"
fi

echo "Creating $ROOT..."
mkdir -p "$ROOT"

########################################
# 1) Top-level build/orchestration files
########################################
cat > "$ROOT/README_INSTALL.md" <<'README'
RealOneOS - build & install instructions
=======================================

This folder contains everything to build a Raspberry Pi image with RealOne pre-installed.

1. Prereqs (on a Linux machine / WSL2)
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install git wget unzip qemu-user-static debootstrap bsdtar xz-utils dosfstools parted rsync curl openssl

2. To create the archive (already done by this script):
   ./make-zip.sh

3. To build an image (high level):
   - Clone official pi-gen: git clone https://github.com/RPi-Distro/pi-gen.git
   - Copy the contents of 'pi-image-build/pi-gen-overlay' into the pi-gen folder:
       cp -r pi-image-build/pi-gen-overlay/* pi-gen/
   - Run the pi-gen build:
       cd pi-gen
       sudo ./build.sh
   - The final image will appear in pi-gen/deploy/

4. After flashing image to SD, boot Pi and follow on-screen RealOne setup wizard.

README

